<title>RUSSIA: Novorossiisk oil pipelines may shut Oct 20 - trade.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk oil pipelines may shut Oct 20 - trade.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two crude oil pipelines feeding Russia's Black Sea oil export outlet of Novorossiisk may close for planned maintenance on October 20, trade sources said on Friday. They said the 800 mm pipeline could shut for 85 hours, while the 500 mm link might close for 56 hours.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the preliminary schedule, and it's always subject to revision,&quot; said a Moscow source.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk often shuts down temporarily due to planned maintenance or strong winds in the winter.</p>
<p>It has a storage capacity of 300,000 metric tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
